The attached image, Figure 9 from the 2015 Journal of Controlled Release article, illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the antibody response to adsorbed antigens. Mice injected with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) formulated with Nano-11 at various doses (50, 200, 800 µg/dose) developed significantly higher anti-rPA IgG titers compared to rPA alone (*p < 0.01). This demonstrates Nano-11's strong adjuvant effect on antibody responses in vivo, with comparable or superior efficacy to aluminum hydroxide at similar antigen doses, supporting its potential as an effective vaccine delivery vehicle.